From 622135e99973b22fabb5faa1a62802b69c080a14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:32:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: xradio: Drop the vif lock when a TX confirm finds no
 queued packet

xrwl_hwpriv_to_vifpriv() returns with priv->vif_lock held, and every path
of xradio_tx_confirm_cb() must release it. When xradio_queue_get_skb()
fails, neither the requeue branch nor the success branch runs, and the
function returns with the lock held. That happens when the firmware
confirms a frame that a deauth already flushed (the WARN at
xradio_queue_get_skb). The next wsm_get_tx() in the bh thread then spins on
the lock forever. The resulting RCU stall wedges deauth
(synchronize_rcu_expedited), rtnl users (iw, ip) and even mount.

Seen on the TrimUI Smart Pro when switching from a WPA3 network back to
WPA2 during traffic. Two connect/disconnect rounds with a ping flood
during the disconnect now pass without a hang. The late-confirm path did
not trigger in those rounds, so the fix is verified by code inspection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/xradio/tx.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/tx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/tx.c
index a070b6aa9..1c4ec2074 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/tx.c
@@ -1286,6 +1286,14 @@ void xradio_tx_confirm_cb(struct xradio_common *hw_priv,
 		
 
 		xradio_queue_remove(queue, arg->packetID);
+	} else {
+		/*
+		 * The packet is gone from the queue (flushed on deauth, for
+		 * example) and the firmware confirmed it late. The vif lock
+		 * taken by xrwl_hwpriv_to_vifpriv() must still be dropped,
+		 * otherwise the next wsm_get_tx() spins on it forever.
+		 */
+		spin_unlock(&priv->vif_lock);
 	}
 }
 
